      "writtenOn": "2018-10-19T14:53:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the over current scenario is rare, I would lean toward having the delay all the time to make the code more simple. (I think we could get rid of the clear_oc_event_att stuff entirely).\n\nI think it is reasonable for us to implement a cool-down of the port when OC happens. If the user tries another dongle, the port will be re-enabled by the time that they get it.\n\nIs a wait period of 1-second enough? how quickly does the fake disconnect loop happen?",
      "parentUuid": "937a94fb_2c185c29",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 28
